import tests/games/studio/session.dl
import tests/games/studio/viewport.dl

the spatial study in {a pointer to UI instance:instance} means: instance's state as a pointer to spatial session
this spatial study means: the spatial study in this window

to paint a spatial study on {a pointer to UI canvas frame:canvas}:
    set session to the spatial study in (canvas's instance)
    set frame to canvas's frame
    set state to frame's window as a pointer to DynlexGraphics
    set projection to state's projection
    set camera to state's camera
    set model to state's model
    set depth to state's depth_testing
    draw a rounded UI surface (canvas's bounds) with radius 0.0 from (session's background) to (session's background) opacity 255 feathered by 0.0 on frame
    use viewport (the framebuffer box of (canvas's bounds) in (session's view as a pointer to native UI view)) on frame
    set state's model to an identity graphics matrix
    @intrinsic("call pointer", session's painter, nothing, canvas)
    set state's projection to projection
    set state's camera to camera
    set state's model to model
    set state's depth_testing to depth
    restore the viewport on frame

to use a perspective of {floating-point number:angle} degrees from {floating-point number:near} to {floating-point number:far} on {a pointer to UI canvas frame:canvas}:
    set state to canvas's frame's window as a pointer to DynlexGraphics
    set state's projection to a graphics perspective projection with angle angle aspect (canvas's bounds' width / canvas's bounds' height) near near far far
    enable depth testing in (canvas's frame)

window spatial studio:
    group at 32 24 sized 720 by 64:
        brand "SPATIAL STUDIO"
        caption "A DIFFERENT POINT OF VIEW"
    group at 1012 32 sized 236 by 40:
        badge "View status"
    panel at 344 112 sized 904 by 600:
        group at 24 20 sized 856 by 20:
            eyebrow "EXPLORE IN THREE DIMENSIONS"
        canvas "Scene" at 24 64 sized 856 by 480
        group at 24 564 sized 856 by 20:
            caption "W / S  FORWARD / BACK     A / D  STRAFE     Q / E  ALTITUDE     ARROWS  TURN"
    panel at 32 112 sized 288 by 600:
        eyebrow "CHANGE YOUR PERSPECTIVE"
        space of 12 pixels
        title "Room to"
        accent title "explore."
        space of 12 pixels
        statistic "Scene name"
        primary button "Reset camera"
        button "Pause / resume"
        space of 12 pixels
        caption "Move freely. Take a closer look."
    group at 56 568 sized 240 by 112:
        caption "R resets the camera."
        caption "P pauses navigation and animation."
    group at 32 736 sized 1216 by 20:
        caption "P  PAUSE     R  RESET VIEW     TAB + ENTER  NAVIGATE     ESC  CLOSE"
    style:
        the interface uses a "midnight" theme
        the interface fits 1280 by 780 pixels
        the window is at least 960 by 585 pixels
    code:
        when the "Reset camera" button is clicked:
            restart this spatial study
        when the "Pause / resume" button is clicked:
            set this spatial study's paused to not this spatial study's paused
        when painting the "Scene" canvas:
            paint a spatial study on this canvas
